===Etymology===
From {{inh|mk|sla-pro|*sę}}, from {{inh|mk|ine-bsl-pro|*sen}}, from {{inh|mk|ine-pro|*swé}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{mk-IPA}}
* {{homophones|mk|сѐ}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|mk|pronoun form}}

# {{n-g|Short reflexive direct object pronoun (all persons).}}
# {{lb|mk|reflexive pronoun|clitic}} the accusative short form of the [[reflexive pronoun]] ''[[себе си]]'', part of [[reflexive verbs]], denoting that the subject is simultaneously the direct object; corresponds to [[myself]], [[yourself]], [[himself]], [[herself]], [[itself]], [[ourselves]], [[yourselves]], [[themselves]]
#: {{ux|mk|'''Се''' [[сакам]].|I love '''myself'''.}}
#: {{ux|mk|'''Се''' [[сака]].|He/she/it loves '''himself'''/'''herself'''/'''itself'''.}}
# {{lb|mk|reciprocal pronoun|clitic}} accusative [[reciprocal pronoun]], denoting that the agents perform the mutual actions among themselves; corresponds to [[each other]], [[one another]]
#: {{ux|mk|Марија [[и]] Петар '''се''' [[сакаат]].|Maria and Petar love '''each other'''.}}
# {{lb|mk|reflexive pronoun|clitic}} [[reflexive pronoun]], part of [[w:Autocausative verb|autocausative verbs]], denoting that the referent represented by the subject combines the activity of actor and undergoes a change of state like a patient
#: {{ux|mk|Петар '''се''' [[навреди]].|Peter became offended.}}
# {{lb|mk|reflexive pronoun|clitic}} [[reflexive pronoun]], part of [[w:Anticausative verb|anticausative verbs]], denoting that the subject of the verb undergoes an action or change of state whose agent is unclear or nonexistent
#: {{ux|mk|[[вратата|Вратата]] '''се''' [[отвори]].|The door was opened.}}
# {{lb|mk|reflexive pronoun|clitic}} used for passive constructions with transitive verbs and undetermined agent
#: {{ux|mk|[[од|Од]] [[мојата]] [[куќа]] '''се''' [[гледа]] [[морето]].|From my house one can see the sea.}}
#: {{ux|mk|'''Се''' [[вели]], [[дека]]...|It is said that...}}
# {{lb|mk|reflexive pronoun|clitic|formal}} used for passive constructions with transitive verbs and determined agent
#: {{ux|mk|[[куќата|Куќата]] '''се''' [[проектира]] [[од]] [[познат]] [[архитект]].|The house was designed by a famous architect.}}
# {{lb|mk|reflexive pronoun|clitic}} inherent part of an [[unergative]] reflexive or reciprocal verb with no meaning of its own, and an obligatory part of the verb's lexical entry
#: {{ux|mk|[[јас|Јас]] '''се''' [[се гордее|гордеам]] [[со]] [[школскиот]] [[успех]] [[на]] Иво.|I am proud of Ivo's success as school.}}
#: {{ux|mk|[[таа|Таа]] '''се''' [[се надева|надева]] [[дека]] [[ќе]] [[освои]] [[златен]] [[медал]].|She is hoping to win the gold medal.}}

